CORE
main.c
--datarace --no-assertions --no-por --unwind 2 --rounds 2 --allow-pointer-unsoundness
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
A heap array of symbolic size is one object; a race on it pairs accesses by
element. main reads datas[0] converted to int (return datas[0]); the cast
hid the element from the offset finder, the read kept offset -1 and never
paired with the thread's write of element 0 (per-thread-array-join-counter-
race-4, no-data-race, expected false).
